# foldsim_ctrl_check's design total: past --max-total a REFUSE (the FSD calibration's default); with --calibration
# and --family the family's own total from its built images and its verdict past it (WARN at small scale), reported.
# RUN: not python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_ctrl_check.py %S/Inputs/ctrl-check/sim.sv --max-total 5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REF
# RUN: python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_ctrl_check.py %S/Inputs/ctrl-check/sim.sv --calibration %S/Inputs/ctrl-check/cal.json --family small-routed | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WARN
# RUN: python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_ctrl_check.py %S/Inputs/ctrl-check/sim.sv --calibration %S/Inputs/ctrl-check/cal.json --family big | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OK
# RUN: not python3 %foldsim_tools/foldsim_ctrl_check.py %S/Inputs/ctrl-check/sim.sv --calibration %S/Inputs/ctrl-check/cal.json --family nope 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOFAM
# REF: predicted LUT-RAM write-enable control sets 6
# REF: REFUSE: 6 predicted control sets > max total 5
# WARN: WARN: 6 predicted control sets > max total 5 (family small-routed: a routed point of 5)
# OK: total 6 within 100 (family big: a routed point of 100)
# OK-NOT: REFUSE
# NOFAM: no family 'nope'
